      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Prior to the latest update, I also tested both the Steam and Oculus builds of VRChat over Virtual Desktop, and found that the Oculus version usually had a higher framerate and was much less likely to cause motion sickness for me.\nWhile I understand what VRChat is attempting to do with this update, it's a huge disappointment to be told to use the Steam version when I know in the past I've had to pull my headset off mid-session with it to avoid hurling.  And Air Link has the problems noted by timduru above.  All in all, the options I'm being directed towards are inferior to what I had before.\nHaving VD no longer work with the Oculus build of VRChat seems like an unintended consequence since VD is not a mod, so I'd like to see VRChat take steps to remediate this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
